@{
    ViewBag.Title = "About";
}
<main aria-labelledby="title">
    <h2 id="title">About Application</h2>
    

   
    <p>
        <b> Contoso University</b> – Application Overview
        <br />

        Contoso University is a sample web application built to demonstrate the features and best practices of a modern ASP.NET MVC application. It simulates a simple university management system and provides functionality for managing students, courses, instructors, departments, and enrollments.

        The application is  used as a teaching tool and reference project for learning ASP.NET MVC, Entity Framework, and general web development practices in the .NET ecosystem.<br/>

        🧩 Key Features<br/>

        📚 Student Management: Create, edit, and view student records.<br/>

        🧑‍🏫 Instructor Management: Assign instructors to courses and manage office assignments.<br/>

        🏫 Department Management: Handle department data and administrator assignments.<br/>

        📖 Course Enrollment: Enroll students in courses and manage grades.<br/>

        🔍 Sorting, Filtering, Paging: Easy-to-use UI for navigating large data sets.<br/>

        📊 Reporting: Simple reporting of student enrollments and course assignments.<br/>

        🛠️ Technologies Used<br>

        ASP.NET MVC (Model-View-Controller)<br/>

        1.Entity Framework (Code First)<br/>

        2.SQL Server (LocalDB or full SQL Server)<br/>

        3.Bootstrap (for responsive UI)<br/>

        Razor View Engine<br/>

        🎯 Purpose<br/>

        The purpose of the Contoso University application is to serve as a reference architecture and learning project for developers working with:<br/>

        1. ASP.NET MVC/Web Applications<br/>

        2.Data access using Entity Framework<br/>

        3.UI development using Razor and Bootstrap<br/>

        4.Real-world application structure and best practices
    </p>
</main>